WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.630
- Okay, if an asteroid
were coming to hit earth.

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:05.463
- Yeah.

00:00:05.463 --> 00:00:06.296
- [Kelly] Like the movies.

00:00:06.296 --> 00:00:07.129
- How would we stop it?

00:00:07.129 --> 00:00:07.962
I mean, this is possible, right?

00:00:07.962 --> 00:00:08.795
- Oh yes, so.

00:00:08.795 --> 00:00:10.014
We know exactly how to stop it.

00:00:10.014 --> 00:00:10.847
- He knows the answer right!

00:00:10.847 --> 00:00:13.133
- No, no, no, it's only
two ways you can stop it.

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:15.190
One of them is the macho way.

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:16.023
- Blow it up?

00:00:16.023 --> 00:00:17.440
- Blow the sucker out of the sky.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.411
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:18.411 --> 00:00:19.244
- Okay.

00:00:19.244 --> 00:00:20.294
- I'm from the south.

00:00:20.294 --> 00:00:21.304
(laughing)

00:00:21.304 --> 00:00:22.823
- You uttered all those--

00:00:22.823 --> 00:00:23.881
- -[Kelly] Shoot it!

00:00:23.881 --> 00:00:25.100
- Oh yeah, shoot the
sucker out of the sky!

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.369
- Who cares what the
ramifications to the rest of

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:28.202
the universe are.

00:00:28.202 --> 00:00:29.322
- This is what I'm saying.

00:00:29.322 --> 00:00:30.155
- Yeah.

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:33.098
- In America, we now blow stuff
up, but we don't always know

00:00:33.098 --> 00:00:34.770
where the pieces go!

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.680
'cause we blow it up,
now can have two parts

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:37.513
that are gonna hit.

00:00:37.513 --> 00:00:38.460
All the pieces, what's gonna happen?

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.660
So kind of a gentler
way is you go up there

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.980
and you nudge it out of harms way.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.640
If you get there early
enough, you nudge it a little,

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.300
that accumulates and then
it misses earth entirely.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.630
- What are you nudging it with?

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:50.993
- That's a good question!

00:00:50.993 --> 00:00:52.160
(laughing)

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:52.993
- Excuse me!

00:00:52.993 --> 00:00:55.883
- An astronaut goes up there
and goes, "There we go."

00:00:55.883 --> 00:00:57.737
(laughing)

00:00:57.737 --> 00:01:00.580
- So there are ways you
can do it gravitationally,

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.410
what we call a gravitational tether.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.170
So you have another object
and they attract each other,

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:06.825
and so as they attract each other--

00:01:06.825 --> 00:01:07.658
- Like a magnet?

00:01:07.658 --> 00:01:09.620
- Well, like with gravity, so, yeah.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:10.498
Gravity.

00:01:10.498 --> 00:01:11.331
- A gravity tether.

00:01:11.331 --> 00:01:12.164
- Gravity tether.

00:01:12.164 --> 00:01:12.997
- Gravity tether, that's
what, I knew that.

00:01:12.997 --> 00:01:14.038
You should explain it to her, I know!

00:01:14.038 --> 00:01:15.330
(laughing)

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.460
- So they attack each
other but then this object

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.840
you put up there has
rockets in that pulls aside,

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:22.290
and they still attract
each other and it slowly

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.940
drags it out of harms way.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:24.970
There will be a gravitational action.

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:26.570
- That would have been a
much easier answer than

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:27.560
all those movies.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:28.393
- Yeah.

00:01:28.393 --> 00:01:30.300
- Then you don't get to flood
New York and stuff like that.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.133
- Right, right.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.170
- Well it would have to be fun too!

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:33.003
- So here's the twist--

00:01:33.003 --> 00:01:34.464
- Or you could just blow it up!

00:01:34.464 --> 00:01:35.950
- We know how to do it
from an engineering point,

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:39.080
but there is no funded project
in the world to actually

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:39.920
make that happen.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.900
So we are just sitting ducks!

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.060
- [Kelly] Oh my god!

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:45.092
- I'm fretting ain't it great!

00:01:45.092 --> 00:01:46.558
(laughing)

00:01:46.558 --> 00:01:47.391
- Sorry we're all gonna die!

00:01:47.391 --> 00:01:48.932
(laughing)

00:01:48.932 --> 00:01:49.765
- He's kidding!

00:01:49.765 --> 00:01:51.220
- Who am I kidding.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:52.789
- We need you to become engineers

00:01:52.789 --> 00:01:54.735
so you can solve this problem.

00:01:54.735 --> 00:01:55.760
- Yes that's right!

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:56.593
(clapping)

00:01:56.593 --> 00:01:58.328
- [Kelly] With gravitational tether.

